<p>India and the United Arab Emirates signed defence and energy agreements on Friday during Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s visit to Abu Dhabi, India’s foreign ministry said. The announcements included a strategic defence partnership framework, agreements on strategic petroleum reserves and liquefied petroleum gas, and cooperation between ADNOC and Indian energy companies. Ahead of the visit, Indian sources told Reuters Modi was expected to discuss long-term energy supply deals and support for expanding India’s emergency oil storage capacity. UAE President Sheikh Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan hosted Modi for talks. India said UAE investment commitments totaled about $5 billion, including deals linked to infrastructure and financial firms.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/SsgRt3XRxen-DCUVcCABTWLDLxzAd1d1BFyTNLXaPOU3s9l0lGnH6oBcOLAk05tQY1IrXbyl4TeY30t-V5n_EU1Ko_DBks4k-aD69k7rkJM-' alt='President of the United Arab Emirates, Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan, meets Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi during an official visit reception in Abu Dhabi on May 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Visit schedule: Modi began a five-nation tour in Abu Dhabi, with later stops in the Netherlands, Sweden, Norway and Italy.</li><li>Brief stop: Some reports said the UAE leg lasted only a few hours before Modi continued to Europe.</li><li>Indian diaspora: Modi thanked Sheikh Mohamed for looking after the Indian community in the UAE during what he called challenging times.</li><li>Hormuz remarks: Modi said keeping the Strait of Hormuz “free, open and safe” was India’s highest priority after meeting Sheikh Mohamed.</li></ul><blockquote>India’s scale and growth trajectory make it one of the defining energy markets of our time. As demand accelerates alongside a rapidly expanding population, the strength of the UAE India energy partnership becomes ever more critical - Sultan Ahmed Al Jaber</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Indian foreign ministry: The ministry announced the defence framework and energy agreements during Modi’s visit and described them as part of deeper bilateral ties during the Iran war. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/2000469/india-uae-agree-on-framework-for-strategic-defence-partnership-during-modi-visit'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>ADNOC: The UAE state oil company said the agreements with Indian energy companies covered crude oil, gas storage and strategic reserves, along with LPG supply and trading opportunities with Indian Oil Corporation. (<a href='https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/energy/2026/05/15/adnoc-signs-strategic-agreements-with-indian-energy-companies-during-modis-visit-to-the-uae/'>The National</a>)</li><li>Narendra Modi: Modi condemned attacks on the UAE and said India was ready to extend all possible support for peace in West Asia during his talks in Abu Dhabi. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/india-ready-to-extend-all-possible-support-for-peace-in-west-asia-pm-modi-in-uae/article70982201.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>UAE government: WAM said the leaders also discussed cooperation across economy, investment, energy, space, food security, technology and artificial intelligence, and exchanged views on Middle East developments. (<a href='https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20260515-india-uae-sign-pacts-to-boost-ties-including-in-defense-as-modi-begins-multi-nation-tour/'>Middle East Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/india/640023-india-and-uae-ink-energy/'>India and UAE ink energy and defense pacts</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/2000469/india-uae-agree-on-framework-for-strategic-defence-partnership-during-modi-visit'>India, UAE agree on framework for strategic defence partnership during Modi visit</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/india-ready-to-extend-all-possible-support-for-peace-in-west-asia-pm-modi-in-uae/article70982201.ece'>‘We condemn attacks on UAE’, says PM Modi, signs defence coo